From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:49:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/66] Revert "wifi: ath12k: mark PCI 0x110e as a TME firmware
 image"

This reverts commit b5809da62. The flag only told MHI to send the
second ELF of the peach image over BHIe. 7.3 MHI detects the second
ELF at sbl_size by itself, and the flag is gone from struct
mhi_controller in the 7.3 port of dodge 0008.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
index 3b29052fc..ee87f00bc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -256,12 +256,6 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
 	mhi_ctrl->sbl_size = SZ_512K;
 	mhi_ctrl->seg_len = SZ_512K;
 	mhi_ctrl->fbc_download = true;
-	/*
-	 * PCI 0x110e (peach) firmware is two ELF files. The second one
-	 * starts at sbl_size, and that is what BHIe has to send.
-	 */
-	if (ab_pci->pdev->device == 0x110e)
-		mhi_ctrl->tme_supported_image = true;
 	mhi_ctrl->runtime_get = ath12k_mhi_op_runtime_get;
 	mhi_ctrl->runtime_put = ath12k_mhi_op_runtime_put;
 	mhi_ctrl->status_cb = ath12k_mhi_op_status_cb;
